      "type": "title",
      "value": "Key Design Strategies"
    },
    {
      "type": "description",
      "value": "<ul><li>Embrace nostalgia by updating classic silhouettes with modern practicality for transseasonal, day-to-night versatility.</li><li>Focus on tactile, restorative materials such as soft suede, shearling, pony hair, and plush textures to add newness and a comforting feel.</li><li>Refine core styles with fashion-forward details like pointed or square toes, kitten or architectural block heels, and statement hardware.</li><li>For Biker and Knee Boots, use belts, buckles, and refined leather finishes to create durable, investment-worthy pieces.</li><li>Introduce directional volume through the Slouchy Boot, using soft ruching and gathered constructions in suede or supple leather.</li><li>Update the Ankle Boot with Victorian-inspired lace-up details for a more formal, historical aesthetic.</li></ul>"
    },
